// TPM2_Load is used to load objects into the TPM. TPM2_Load is used when both a
// TPM2B_PUBLIC and TPM2B_PRIVATE are to be loaded. If only a TPM2B_PUBLIC is to
// be loaded, the TPM2_LoadExternal() command is used. The object’s TPMA_OBJECT
// attributes will be checked according to the rules defined in “TPMA_OBJECT” in
// TPM 2.0 Part 2 of this specification.
//
// encryptedDuplication shall be CLEAR if fixedTPM is SET. If fixedTPM is CLEAR,
// then this attribute shall have the same value as its parent, unless fixedTPM
// is SET the parent, in which case, it may be SET or CLEAR.
TpmTestVector(
  name: "[TPM2_Load] encryptedDuplication not consistent with template",
  spec_versions: [
    184,
  ],
  test_sequence: [
  ]
)
